hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1521","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Abi Hazim told us, my father told me, on the authority of Sahl, that a group of people came to him who were exercising in the pulpit from... Which oud is it? And who made it? Sahl said: By God, I know what stick it is from, and who made it, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the first day he rose upon it. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to so-and-so and said: He will name her that day, and I forgot her name: “Let your servant, the carpenter, work for me.” “sticks on which I speak to people.” So he made these three steps from the edge of the forest, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rise up over him. So he said “Allahu Akbar,” and the people behind him said “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed, and the people bowed, then he rose and descended backwards, then he prostrated at the beginning of the pulpit, then he returned until he finished. He completed his last prayer, then he turned to them and said: “I have only done this so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.”"
"1522","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, and he mentioned the hadith, but he did not say: “I only did this so that you would follow me. And they learned my prayer.”"
